## Band Description

Meridian Chord Office is a four-member acoustic-electric ensemble built around the principle that a fretted chord can exist physically before it exists acoustically.

**Klara Weiss** — arpeggione, Fret Transfer design, left-hand chord geometry, bow-order architecture.

**Marcus Vale** — drum machine, palm-muted electric bass, Hidden Chord arrangement, groove structure.

**Élodie Marchand** — prepared Rhodes, delayed harmonic replies, chord-shell voicings.

**Nico Brandt** — bass trumpet, low brass punctuation, Full-Grip Flash reinforcement.

There is no conventional frontperson. Klara defines the chord shape and decides how it becomes audible; Marcus controls what the rhythm section is permitted to reveal at each stage; Élodie confirms or complicates newly exposed tones; Nico marks structural moments where partial harmony becomes complete. Live versions vary because string tension, bow hair, fret pressure, bow speed, and the exact sequence of string crossings alter the timing and weight of every transfer.

